      "lineNbr": 2972,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-01T16:10:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, if we don\u0027t set it back to false, then the next async transaction (or this one on the retry) will assume that there is a pending_async transaction when there isn\u0027t one and everything will queue on async_todo with none ever getting dequeued and posted to the proc-\u003etodo.\n\nThe alternative would be to remove this line and change the logic at 2933 to\n  if (oneway \u0026\u0026 !retry)\n\nso pending_async is preserved as false and this transaction gets queued on proc-\u003etodo. That might be a nice simplification.\n\nI was a little nervous about letting node-\u003ehas_async_transaction \u003d\u003d true when the node-\u003elock is dropped if there isn\u0027t actually an async transaction in flight...",
      "parentUuid": "808a5928_0fc3ed4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2971,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2972,
        "endChar": 40
